WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.420
<v Mike>The Cryon Conquest.

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:05.120
<v Mike>If you are out there, please come.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:30.120
<v Mike>And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.260
<v Hosts>I'm Mike.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.280
<v Hosts>I'm Sean. And I'm Joe.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.800
<v Mike>Thanks for coming, guys.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:36.060
<v Sean>I didn't have any of you here.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:39.680
<v Sean>We were out there. You heeded the call.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.960
<v Mike>So I guess we'll do this episode?

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:50.900
<v Sean>Yeah. I've got my wizard hat and wand and I'm ready to go.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.020
<v Joe>Broom. Easily controllable broom.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.840
<v Mike>Sean, are you a magical girl?

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.420
<v Sean>I'm so magic, bro.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.380
<v Mike>That's pretty banging.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.120
<v Mike>Right? That's straight bussing, Sean.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.320
<v Joe>I'm Francesca.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:08.100
<v Mike>That's actually what she says at the beginning of the game.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.160
<v Joe>And that explains everything we need to know.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:11.140
<v Mike>She says, I am Francesca.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.020
<v Sean>Yeah. Let's just get right down to brass tacks real quick.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:23.240
<v Sean>Like, first of all, this is a carbon copy of like the setup from last week's episode where like robots attack the earth and stuff.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.380
<v Mike>But in robots attacking the earth is so hot.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.760
<v Sean>It's so hot right now.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:41.440
<v Sean>And instead of, you know, finding some 25 year old expendable like military man to copy his brain waves and enter the, enter the matrix, you just summon a witch.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.820
<v Sean>And she says, I'm Francesca.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:50.600
<v Sean>But she also kind of has like the facial expression of Kevin James in that meme.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:52.500
<v Sean>Like when she says it. Right.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:54.760
<v Mike>But let me ask you something.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.560
<v Mike>Would you rather she say happy birthday?

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.060
<v Mike>Like Frosty the snowman, right?

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.900
<v Mike>Isn't it a little better to just say your name when you, when you introduce yourself?

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.080
<v Mike>I am Francesca.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:06.120
<v Mike>And then they just cut away.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.920
<v Sean>Yeah. Everything she says after that is not, not, not pertinent.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:11.960
<v Joe>Yeah. I'm like not even sure.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.700
<v Joe>Like I needed her to say something more.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.640
<v Joe>I just needed to know like, where did she come from?

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:17.880
<v Joe>How did this guy summon her?

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.140
<v Joe>Like what's going on?

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:27.240
<v Mike>Like just at all. Legally, legally she has to say I am Francesca so that the people at Capcom don't think she's Mega Man.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:36.300
<v Mike>That's true. That's going to be a huge problem in this week's episode is that we are basically playing a lawsuit.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.560
<v Mike>I don't know how they got away with this one, but they did.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:44.040
<v Mike>This is a, this is a Mega Man clone.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:45.580
<v Mike>Arguably the first, right?

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.240
<v Mike>I don't think we've seen anything come this close.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:55.980
<v Mike>I mean, technically just last week, again, we did have a game where like you gained a new power every time you beat a boss, but that's not like that's not lawsuit worthy.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.760
<v Mike>That's just kind of like a good idea.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.360
<v Sean>Yeah, it's not even in this game.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.480
<v Mike>Right, right. In this game, you just have them all.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:05.960
<v Mike>It's like, forget, forget going to different places to get your powers.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.380
<v Mike>What if you just started all of them?

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:08.840
<v Mike>This game's better than Mega Man.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:17.080
<v Mike>Well, maybe we should decide that over the course of the episode, preferably at the end of the episode, if you don't mind, if you guys could just wait till then.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:18.660
<v Mike>Yeah, sorry. We blew it there.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.400
<v Mike>You guys talked. Thank you.

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:24.000
<v Mike>The pitch, it's 1999.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:27.560
<v Mike>It's not really that.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.820
<v Mike>It's 1991 in chronological.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.300
<v Mike>It's 2026. It's 2026 here.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.620
<v Mike>But it's 1999 in the game.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.960
<v Mike>And as Sean mentioned, aliens are attacking Earth.

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:47.180
<v Mike>An alien robot empire called the Cryons have invaded Earth and their forces are immune to every conventional weapon.

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:48.760
<v Sean>Tanks, missiles.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.680
<v Mike>The whole military playbook is out the window.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:57.760
<v Mike>That's all we got. Except the one thing that we have yet to figure out how to monetize.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:59.280
<v Sean>Money. Magic.

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:02.180
<v Sean>What? Magic.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:06.060
<v Mike>And magic is not something that we have yet.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:09.020
<v Mike>The solution, of course, find a witch.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.540
<v Mike>Enter I am Francesca, a young witch for hire.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:17.360
<v Mike>Apparently the only practitioner of magic in the world.

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:19.400
<v Mike>But this world seems to have magic.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:27.780
<v Sean>Right? I mean, if it's not magic that brought her there, like, I mean, that does imply that there might be other magic aside from her.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.140
<v Mike>Right? Yeah, I assume so.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:36.460
<v Mike>So maybe I'm implying that she's the only practitioner of magic, but she's certainly the only one looking to save the day.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:47.320
<v Mike>So she sets out alone to use her magic to dismantle the Cryon Empire through basically four stages.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:48.520
<v Mike>Anything I missed?

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:50.500
<v Joe>No, that's it. That's the game.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:51.620
<v Mike>Oh, great. That's the game. Yeah, yeah.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:56.200
<v Sean>So the Mega Man stuff, like, it is true.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:58.460
<v Sean>This feels very Mega Man.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:04.700
<v Sean>I'm pretty sure they traced Mega Man's sprite and then just put, like, a witch hat on it.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:09.420
<v Sean>The whole, like, the health works the same.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:16.100
<v Sean>The powers kind of work the same, but there's no, like, ammunition to them.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:20.500
<v Joe>Even when you die, it looks exactly the same.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.640
<v Sean>Yeah, you explode the same way.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:36.000
<v Sean>It's really blatant. But, like, all that being said, this game does feel different because, like, it's so much more based on how you get around the stage.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:37.920
<v Sean>Like, I feel like...

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:43.980
<v Mike>That is true. There's a lot of navigating and there's a lot of constantly switching your weapons.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:51.860
<v Mike>Like, in Mega Man, it's kind of a, oh, I know that the boss is weak to this, so I'm going to use this power-up that I acquired in the previous stage.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:58.600
<v Mike>This game notably does not have a stage select screen at all, so you don't get to choose, like, which one you're going to tackle first.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:00.360
<v Mike>So it's missing that from Mega Man.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:06.740
<v Mike>But then, yes, I agree with you, Sean, that it is a lot of times you have to use the broom power.

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:07.660
<v Sean>The goddamn broom. Yeah.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:14.420
<v Mike>To propel yourself forward because the other option is to just jump into a pile of spikes.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:18.740
<v Mike>There is no reasonable way to jump otherwise across these platforms.

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:20.460
<v Mike>You have to use the broom to navigate.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:29.920
<v Mike>And the broom kind of works like how you would expect Mega Man's dog to work in, like, you know, that it acts as a platform that can be a spring.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.320
<v Mike>Mega Man's dog. Mega Man's dog's name is what?

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.760
<v Mike>Rush. Rush?

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:37.060
<v Mike>Rush is the girl.

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:39.300
<v Mike>Yeah. Sorry, I didn't know.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:40.420
<v Sean>I don't even like Mega Man.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:45.480
<v Mike>I know that. Yeah, I mean, like, would you say my dog's full name to other people or would you say Mike's dog?

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:50.060
<v Sean>Well, I'd say Phoebe just to foster confusion.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:56.280
<v Mike>Okay, great. So now everybody knows my dog's name is Phoebe and they can just say Phoebe and pour her out of the house.

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:58.860
<v Mike>Yeah. Wait, who told you that?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.820
<v Mike>I know it. But we're getting a little ahead of ourselves.

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.700
<v Mike>I just want to bring us back a second.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:10.020
<v Mike>This was a game developed by friend of the show, Vic Takai.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.940
<v Mike>And it's been a minute since we had Vic on the show.

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:18.280
<v Mike>But in Japan, this game, just like last week's episode, I'm seeing a lot of parallels here.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:20.260
<v Mike>It was a different game.

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:22.420
<v Mike>It was Magical Kids Doropy.

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:30.980
<v Joe>Yeah. And was that, that was, I read and I didn't confirm that it was based on Wizard of Oz?

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:31.860
<v Mike>Correct.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:44.880
<v Mike>The wonderful Wizard of Oz, which is why the protagonist name is Doropy, because that is a literal Japanese translation of Dorothy using their kanji.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:48.980
<v Joe>So in this original version, was it still about like robots attacking?

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:52.760
<v Mike>Of course. Who's the Tin Man, but a robot?

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.220
<v Joe>That's a great point.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:57.160
<v Sean>Yeah. That's who you're fighting.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:58.000
<v Mike>The Tin Man and all those friends.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.480
<v Sean>You're fighting the Tin Man. Yeah.

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:03.980
<v Mike>And then, you know, here's a weird thing.

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:09.980
<v Mike>The Wikipedia section, it's an odd claim, and it leads to a dead link.

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:11.720
<v Mike>So who knows if this ever even is true.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:24.020
<v Mike>But it claims that some of the developers for Victikae objected to having a girl as the protagonist because they believed the NES was for boys and players couldn't relate to a female lead.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.880
<v Mike>I did read that. It just feels like a weird thing to include without a source.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:30.220
<v Sean>And then they mentioned something about like eyebrows, which I thought was funny.

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:32.500
<v Sean>Not eyebrows. I didn't even feel like including that.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:39.040
<v Sean>Yeah. And I was like, some weird fan must have just put this information here.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:42.040
<v Sean>This is a part where I do not trust Wikipedia.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.160
<v Mike>Right. It's female character erasure.

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:47.080
<v Sean>Yes. No, she's great.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:53.460
<v Sean>Just get rid of them all together. I mean, what did you guys think when you saw the broom?

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:56.680
<v Sean>When I saw the broom as a power, I thought it was like going to be cool.

00:08:56.860 --> 00:08:59.300
<v Sean>Like it was going to be easy to use.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:05.820
<v Joe>Well, when I first like summoned it or whatever, you know, cause it's like a gun that you shoot and then the broom appears.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:14.560
<v Joe>Kind of weird. But the, when the first time I did it, I was like, okay, it's just a platform that can't move that I can use to like jump one extra step.

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:21.180
<v Joe>Took me a very long time to realize that it can move and then much longer time to realize how to make it move.

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:22.480
<v Joe>It was just like move.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:25.220
<v Mike>And then I, and move in different directions.

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:29.760
<v Joe>Yeah. Right. And it's like, and I, and I'm still not sure I can fully explain it.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:38.000
<v Joe>The gist of it is that like, if you're standing on it, the direction you're facing, once you fire a shot, the broom will move in that direction.

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:44.680
<v Joe>Yeah. But there's like other rules to it that make it like, if you'd like do one thing wrong, it'll disappear and you fall to your death.

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:46.760
<v Mike>And I don't know.

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:47.780
<v Sean>It's a little strange.

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:57.120
<v Sean>It's very strange. So I think Joe and I had a similar like a sequence of discovery where first I just use it as a platform.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:08.500
<v Sean>And it, one, one thing I will give this game credit for is it allows you to be wrong about how the broom works several times before it actually matters.

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:14.480
<v Sean>Right. And so first I thought it was just a platform that you could stand on and jump off of.

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:19.920
<v Sean>And then I realized, oh, you shoot in a direction and it goes that way, but you then just keeps going that way.

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:23.840
<v Mike>And so like, okay, so it's like a single use, like moving platform.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:38.740
<v Sean>And then you realize that if you then continue to shoot in different directions other than down, it can move in those directions and you can kind of like thread it through some platforming needles and yada, yada.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:44.140
<v Sean>But then you will also just randomly fall off because you also free walk around it.

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:57.320
<v Sean>But, um, so I had a lot of like, it's, I, I really dig the, the idea of this broom and how they're sort of integrating it into the level design.

00:10:57.540 --> 00:11:09.600
<v Sean>And like a lot of the segments of these levels are mini puzzles about using the broom, but it's almost like the game is too much about the broom and the broom is too hard to control for it to be that.

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:11.060
<v Sean>I don't know. I'm done.

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:18.200
<v Joe>Yeah. She's a witch. Well, why can't it just be just one press of left on the D pad makes it start going left.

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:20.540
<v Mike>One press of up on the D pad makes it start going up.

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:22.540
<v Sean>Like that's just because you move as well.

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:26.140
<v Joe>Yeah. But why not just not have that be, but then what would you do?

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:27.620
<v Mike>Like wait till you collide with something?

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:29.680
<v Sean>No, just jump. You're off the broom.

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:32.440
<v Mike>Hey, hey, look at this guy.

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:35.320
<v Sean>Video game problem. Game developer job.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:40.240
<v Mike>Which, well, what's funny is also like, you know, we're talking so much about the broom there.

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:49.460
<v Mike>You have six spells in total, but I think it is right to focus on the broom because it's not even that it helps like get around the stages.

00:11:49.460 --> 00:11:51.460
<v Mike>It's necessary to get around the stages.

00:11:51.640 --> 00:12:06.460
<v Mike>And a lot of times they will make it so that you basically have to thread the needle using the broom where it's like very specifically like make sure you spawn the broom in this particular spot or else you will just collide with the wall and fall into the spiked pit.

00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:20.740
<v Mike>And that ultimately becomes like a different kind of game than the rest of this game, which is very much like a Mega Man inspired shooter, you know, against a bunch of enemies and giving you creative solutions for that.

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:25.120
<v Mike>Because the rest of this game has like you have you have a normal shot.

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:26.360
<v Mike>You have your freeze shot.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:28.860
<v Mike>You have your bouncing ball shot.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:38.740
<v Mike>And they teach you about these things pretty like in a friendly way where there's an enemy very early on that just constantly is throwing projectiles.

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:51.900
<v Mike>And if you know, there's just no way to get around it, you you have to figure out like, I think I need to figure out a way to shoot this guy and you try to shoot up and there's a wall in the way and then eventually you're like, oh, I have this bouncing ball thing.

00:12:51.900 --> 00:13:02.660
<v Mike>Like maybe I could arc it so that I could he can't touch me, but I could hit him and it will work and it feels good even though it's like the most obvious thing when you finally pull it off.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:07.200
<v Mike>The rest the rest of that game, I think sounds great.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:17.740
<v Mike>Then when the broomstick becomes so much of the navigation on top of the like the shooting, it becomes an extra element that I didn't sign up for.

00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:27.480
<v Joe>Yeah, I think the broom overall hurts what is otherwise like a pretty well designed system of like multiple weapons.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:29.680
<v Joe>You know, it's like everything else.

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:35.300
<v Joe>Like I do think, well, most of the other ones have like some thought behind them and they have good uses for them.

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:38.040
<v Joe>And there's there's the good like parts of the level that are designed around them.

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:46.300
<v Joe>But I kind of have a hard time like appreciating those because most of my energy is spent trying to figure out how to use the stupid broom.

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:54.120
<v Mike>Now, there there's no MP or weapon energy meter governing how much you can use of these things.

00:13:54.120 --> 00:14:00.340
<v Mike>You can switch freely and fire as much as you want, except for the that Phoenix power.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:06.140
<v Mike>Right. Which costs a lot of health and is kind of it's not really.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:10.040
<v Mike>Yeah. But yeah, it's not even really like it shouldn't it should be a different button.

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:13.940
<v Mike>It's not really like a projectile power thing.

00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:15.840
<v Mike>It's not it's not like something you should switch into.

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:20.040
<v Mike>It feels like a pretty devastating move, not something you consciously like.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.960
<v Mike>The other ones are all like different projectiles you shoot.

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:26.480
<v Mike>And then this one is just, you know, you what is it?

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:27.780
<v Mike>Pink is the color for that one.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:32.700
<v Mike>And you just turn pink and then you just spawn a Phoenix and cost a bunch of your health.

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:36.760
<v Mike>It's just a confusing like it's not really a power like the other ones.

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:45.720
<v Sean>Well, that's why I like and I was trying to find a way to actually articulate what I was feeling here.

00:14:46.000 --> 00:15:01.380
<v Sean>That's one of the things that makes this game feel like a ROM hack that or like a mod that the only way to make that be a thing that you could do was to fit it into the system that was already put in place by Mega Man.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:06.980
<v Sean>Because otherwise it would be like a press press this button to do your screen clear.

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:08.960
<v Sean>But you only have a couple of those.

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:15.800
<v Sean>But they had to fit it into the weapon select system that's already in Mega Man, which this game is not.

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:20.000
<v Sean>So it feels very derivative because of that.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:30.260
<v Mike>Now, in concept, the having the six spells from the beginning, the six powers and also not having a limit to how much you can use them.

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:35.640
<v Mike>That is a genuine design improvement over Mega Man's model.

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:45.100
<v Mike>Like I'm not saying like in the actual games comparing each other, but just in theory, that is a it reads more friendly to 2026 players.

00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:50.000
<v Mike>Just giving the players the tools right from the beginning and trusting them to figure out the application.

